      "api_error_status": null,
      "result": "`more_itertools.chunked` keeps the leftover items and returns them as a shorter final chunk. It doesn't pad or drop them.\n\n```python\n>>> list(chunked([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], 3))\n[[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7]]\n```\n\nIt has a `strict` parameter. With `strict=True`, a short final chunk raises `ValueError` instead. `strict=True` requires `n` to be set.\n\nIf you want padding or dropping instead, use these:\n- `grouper(iterable, n, incomplete='fill', fillvalue=...)` pads the last group. It also supports `'strict'` and `'ignore'`, and `'ignore'` drops the leftovers.\n- `ichunked` is the lazy version. It yields iterators instead of lists.",
